1
00:00:15,708 --> 00:00:17,708
[opening theme music playing]

2
00:00:43,708 --> 00:00:45,624
MIRACLES OF THE ER

3
00:00:45,625 --> 00:00:47,375
GOOD DOCTOR, BAD DOCTOR

4
00:00:49,458 --> 00:00:50,915
YANG-DA UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

5
00:00:50,916 --> 00:00:53,415
If symptoms such as shock
or convulsions occur,

6
00:00:53,416 --> 00:00:55,207
hemodialysis may be considered.

7
00:00:55,208 --> 00:00:58,415
If he can breathe on his own tomorrow,
he can go home the day after that.

8
00:00:58,416 --> 00:01:01,207
But the most important thing
to distinguish is the toxidromes, got it?

9
00:01:01,208 --> 00:01:02,249
- Uh-huh.
- Mm-hm.

10
00:01:02,250 --> 00:01:03,415
- [Yu-hua] Doctor Lin.
- Hm?

11
00:01:03,416 --> 00:01:04,790
Regarding the question you asked me,

12
00:01:04,791 --> 00:01:06,415
I'll let you know Friday.
That's it for now.

13
00:01:06,416 --> 00:01:08,083
- All right. Thanks, Dr. He.
- Thanks, Dr. He.

14
00:01:08,958 --> 00:01:11,665
Looky here. This all takes me back.

15
00:01:11,666 --> 00:01:14,583
Just like when I was in R1
and everything you showed us.

16
00:01:15,333 --> 00:01:17,040
And now you're a big boy.

17
00:01:17,041 --> 00:01:18,833
[chuckles]

18
00:01:19,625 --> 00:01:21,374
You know you're a real doctor,

19
00:01:21,375 --> 00:01:23,125
when you can teach someone.

20
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:26,375
I hope you all can go on
to train your peers.

21
00:01:27,166 --> 00:01:28,583
Protect them so that...

22
00:01:30,500 --> 00:01:32,666
They can avoid the mistakes I made.

23
00:01:34,125 --> 00:01:35,458
- Mm-hm.
- [chuckles softly]

24
00:01:37,041 --> 00:01:38,165
Goodbye, doctor.

25
00:01:38,166 --> 00:01:39,333
[Chao-i] Bye, Dr. He.

26
00:01:42,041 --> 00:01:44,750
Hey. Did she seem okay to you?

27
00:01:45,333 --> 00:01:47,249
[stammers] A little distracted, maybe.

28
00:01:47,250 --> 00:01:48,833
Why? What's the deal?

29
00:01:49,583 --> 00:01:51,125
Her trial starts today.

30
00:01:51,625 --> 00:01:52,583
Already?

31
00:02:13,500 --> 00:02:14,333
Hey.

32
00:02:17,208 --> 00:02:18,041
Are you okay?

33
00:02:19,666 --> 00:02:20,833
Oh, great.

34
00:02:22,875 --> 00:02:25,250
Are you ready
for your courtroom appearance?

35
00:02:25,666 --> 00:02:26,541
Dr. Chou,

36
00:02:27,166 --> 00:02:28,458
sounds like you're interfering.

37
00:02:34,125 --> 00:02:35,125
[exhales]

38
00:02:39,083 --> 00:02:40,083
About yesterday...

39
00:02:40,750 --> 00:02:42,790
I shouldn't have talked to you like that.

40
00:02:42,791 --> 00:02:43,750
I'm sorry.

41
00:02:49,250 --> 00:02:51,250
Did you see the results
for Tang hsi's mom?

42
00:02:53,208 --> 00:02:54,125
I did.

43
00:02:55,083 --> 00:02:56,582
Then how can you

44
00:02:56,583 --> 00:02:57,916
not publish your paper?

45
00:03:01,250 --> 00:03:02,083
Maybe...

46
00:03:04,291 --> 00:03:05,790
There's an error in my research.

47
00:03:05,791 --> 00:03:07,375
I don't want to fall out
with the Director.

48
00:03:07,916 --> 00:03:09,665
I'm afraid of dragging you,

49
00:03:09,666 --> 00:03:11,000
and our colleagues down.

50
00:03:11,583 --> 00:03:13,208
[somber music playing]

51
00:03:14,958 --> 00:03:16,000
[exhales]

52
00:03:18,875 --> 00:03:20,333
[inhales]

53
00:03:21,291 --> 00:03:23,374
Now, is that why you hesitated

54
00:03:23,375 --> 00:03:25,290
<i>during the pericardiocentesis</i>

55
00:03:25,291 --> 00:03:26,583
<i>on that little boy?</i>

56
00:03:28,083 --> 00:03:30,124
[somber music continues]

57
00:03:30,125 --> 00:03:31,541
[inhales]

58
00:03:37,041 --> 00:03:38,083
[knocks]

59
00:03:41,750 --> 00:03:42,665
Good morning, sir.

60
00:03:42,666 --> 00:03:44,166
I hear you're leaving us.

61
00:03:48,791 --> 00:03:50,666
My family just wants you to know...

62
00:03:51,666 --> 00:03:52,750
Your songs mean a lot to us.

63
00:03:53,375 --> 00:03:54,583
I'm grateful to you.

64
00:03:58,291 --> 00:03:59,791
This is from friends of my dad's.

65
00:04:00,750 --> 00:04:02,000
Visually impaired fans of yours,

66
00:04:02,583 --> 00:04:05,165
who asked their families
to write you some well wishes here,

67
00:04:05,166 --> 00:04:06,125
to cheer you on.

68
00:04:14,166 --> 00:04:15,000
Thank you.

69
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:22,332
[phone ringing]

70
00:04:22,333 --> 00:04:23,790
So this is your patient file...

71
00:04:23,791 --> 00:04:25,415
- Dr. Lin!
- Hey?

72
00:04:25,416 --> 00:04:27,040
- Doctor! You gotta help me!
- What is it?

73
00:04:27,041 --> 00:04:28,540
- You gotta help me!
- Yes?

74
00:04:28,541 --> 00:04:29,457
My friend,

75
00:04:29,458 --> 00:04:30,957
he hurt his hand real bad.

76
00:04:30,958 --> 00:04:32,915
- Where is he? Where is he?
- Please. Please help!

77
00:04:32,916 --> 00:04:34,083
He's out the front!

78
00:04:34,958 --> 00:04:36,750
His hand is stuck in the meat grinder.

79
00:04:37,541 --> 00:04:38,457
[groans]

80
00:04:38,458 --> 00:04:39,624
Can you help him register?

81
00:04:39,625 --> 00:04:41,040
But he-- But he can't.

82
00:04:41,041 --> 00:04:43,290
He's undocumented, no papers.

83
00:04:43,291 --> 00:04:44,416
- [sobs]
- [man 1] Doctor.

84
00:04:45,583 --> 00:04:47,457
- Doctor, please help him.
- Please, doctor.

85
00:04:47,458 --> 00:04:48,832
Wen-chih, get a bed here now!

86
00:04:48,833 --> 00:04:51,082
- Okay!
- [man 2] A-wan. Hold on, buddy.

87
00:04:51,083 --> 00:04:52,582
- A-wan. Come on.
- [Geng-ming] Hurry!

88
00:04:52,583 --> 00:04:54,249
[man 2] You're okay.
You're going to be fine.

89
00:04:54,250 --> 00:04:56,624
- [Geng-ming] Come on!
- [Su-ching] Bed coming through. Watch out!

90
00:04:56,625 --> 00:04:58,707
- Watch out for the bed! Here's the bed.
- Coming through.

91
00:04:58,708 --> 00:05:00,249
- Here!
- Alright, bed's here. On the bed.

92
00:05:00,250 --> 00:05:01,290
[Geng-ming] Here we go.

93
00:05:01,291 --> 00:05:02,957
[Su-ching] Give him some room, be careful.

94
00:05:02,958 --> 00:05:04,374
I need bloods and crossmatching.

95
00:05:04,375 --> 00:05:06,249
Consult with surgery immediately
after X-ray.

96
00:05:06,250 --> 00:05:08,082
[Wen-chih] Okay. Still with us? Come on.

97
00:05:08,083 --> 00:05:11,040
- [Geng-ming] Hey. Hey! Hey!
- [men screaming]

98
00:05:11,041 --> 00:05:12,290
[Yu-hua] He's having a seizure!

99
00:05:12,291 --> 00:05:14,082
- [men] A-wan! A-wan.
- Hurry, resus room now!

100
00:05:14,083 --> 00:05:15,624
[Yu-hua] Come on! Let's get into resus.

101
00:05:15,625 --> 00:05:17,124
[man 1] Somebody help him, please!

102
00:05:17,125 --> 00:05:18,208
[Wen-chih] Come on.

103
00:05:19,291 --> 00:05:21,040
A-wan, hang in there, A-wan.

104
00:05:21,041 --> 00:05:22,750
- [Mr. Lai sobs]
- Yes, I see it.

105
00:05:23,208 --> 00:05:24,250
Wait, wait, wait.

106
00:05:24,958 --> 00:05:26,957
He's an illegal migrant.
He could be a fugitive.

107
00:05:26,958 --> 00:05:29,665
It doesn't matter who he is at this point.
Get out!

108
00:05:29,666 --> 00:05:32,207
- You know it's against our policy!
- [man 1] A-wan! You got it!

109
00:05:32,208 --> 00:05:33,457
[Wen-chih] Come on, let's go!

110
00:05:33,458 --> 00:05:35,165
[man 2] He's gonna be okay.

111
00:05:35,166 --> 00:05:38,416
[indistinct chatter]

112
00:05:40,083 --> 00:05:41,499
[Geng-ming] We've stopped the bleeding.

113
00:05:41,500 --> 00:05:43,832
- [Wen-chih] OR is getting ready.
- [Yu-hua] What are his vitals?

114
00:05:43,833 --> 00:05:45,790
Heart 109, BP 118 over 70.

115
00:05:45,791 --> 00:05:48,000
SAT's 80, blood sugar 126.

116
00:05:48,708 --> 00:05:49,540
Doctor.

117
00:05:49,541 --> 00:05:51,749
Maybe there's another reason
his SATS are so low.

118
00:05:51,750 --> 00:05:52,750
[monitor beeping]

119
00:05:56,208 --> 00:05:58,415
- O2 mask. Wen-chih, draw gasses.
- Okay.

120
00:05:58,416 --> 00:05:59,874
Su-ching, a brain CT

121
00:05:59,875 --> 00:06:01,291
- to rule out anything else.
- Got it.

122
00:06:07,083 --> 00:06:08,708
[intense music playing]

123
00:06:25,875 --> 00:06:26,707
JOHN DOE

124
00:06:26,708 --> 00:06:28,207
CT SCAN IMAGE

125
00:06:28,208 --> 00:06:29,833
[sighs]

126
00:06:33,500 --> 00:06:34,416
Dr. Lin?

127
00:06:35,083 --> 00:06:36,208
Is A-wan all right?

128
00:06:37,041 --> 00:06:37,999
He's stable now.

129
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:40,540
And plastic surgery team
will take care of his hand.

130
00:06:40,541 --> 00:06:42,332
I wanted to ask you something.

131
00:06:42,333 --> 00:06:43,999
What were you guys up to when it happened?

132
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:46,915
Oh, just having a few drinks
at break time.

133
00:06:46,916 --> 00:06:49,791
A-wan doesn't drink,
so he made himself a coffee.

134
00:06:50,291 --> 00:06:53,041
After work,
he said he didn't feel so good.

135
00:06:53,500 --> 00:06:54,708
That's when it happened.

136
00:06:55,333 --> 00:06:56,666
It's normal in tests.

137
00:06:57,291 --> 00:06:58,958
So why is his blood chocolate-colored?

138
00:07:00,041 --> 00:07:01,415
You're saying it's normal

139
00:07:01,416 --> 00:07:02,332
but you look worried?

140
00:07:02,333 --> 00:07:03,708
Mm-hm.

141
00:07:04,750 --> 00:07:05,749
Huh?

142
00:07:05,750 --> 00:07:07,166
Is he going to be okay?

143
00:07:12,291 --> 00:07:14,582
What are the chances
you can get his coffee for me?

144
00:07:14,583 --> 00:07:16,207
Oh. Uh-huh.

145
00:07:16,208 --> 00:07:18,165
- I'll go to the factory now.
- Okay.

146
00:07:18,166 --> 00:07:19,415
Wait.

147
00:07:19,416 --> 00:07:21,791
I can take a video. I'll try and call you.

148
00:07:22,375 --> 00:07:23,208
Okay.

149
00:07:23,625 --> 00:07:24,915
Doctor, it's so strange.

150
00:07:24,916 --> 00:07:27,000
Everything else is normal
but his SATS are still down.

151
00:07:28,291 --> 00:07:29,375
[exhales]

152
00:07:31,125 --> 00:07:31,958
Oh.

153
00:07:32,458 --> 00:07:33,333
Sir?

154
00:07:33,750 --> 00:07:36,000
Can you tell me what happened?
What's your name?

155
00:07:37,041 --> 00:07:38,208
A... A-wan.

156
00:07:38,833 --> 00:07:39,666
[Geng-ming] A-wan.

157
00:07:41,083 --> 00:07:42,540
Oh.

158
00:07:42,541 --> 00:07:44,791
[sobs]

159
00:07:50,166 --> 00:07:51,665
You'll be taken care of here, okay?

160
00:07:51,666 --> 00:07:53,165
You'll need an operation.

161
00:07:53,166 --> 00:07:54,458
Are you in pain anywhere else?

162
00:07:56,333 --> 00:07:57,832
My head...

163
00:07:57,833 --> 00:07:59,333
It hurts a lot.

164
00:08:00,250 --> 00:08:01,291
Just hypoxia?

165
00:08:01,916 --> 00:08:04,291
[A-wan groaning]

166
00:08:09,750 --> 00:08:12,208
[grunts]

167
00:08:13,166 --> 00:08:14,207
Let's use an NRM.

168
00:08:14,208 --> 00:08:15,125
Right.

169
00:08:17,958 --> 00:08:20,165
- Ah, A-Wan.
- [grunts nervously]

170
00:08:20,166 --> 00:08:21,875
Look at you hiding over here.

171
00:08:22,833 --> 00:08:24,375
Um... And you are?

172
00:08:24,916 --> 00:08:25,790
Who me?

173
00:08:25,791 --> 00:08:27,499
I'm from Zhongda Agency.

174
00:08:27,500 --> 00:08:29,041
His employer reported him gone.

175
00:08:29,541 --> 00:08:30,582
He's accused of theft.

176
00:08:30,583 --> 00:08:32,749
- He's a runaway migrant.
- [grunts nervously]

177
00:08:32,750 --> 00:08:34,291
We'll take him back now.

178
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:37,458
Hey, you can't take him now.

179
00:08:38,083 --> 00:08:38,915
Looks fine to me.

180
00:08:38,916 --> 00:08:41,875
Can't you just patch him up
and pull out the needles? Huh?

181
00:08:42,416 --> 00:08:44,332
Hey, stop! He still needs surgery!

182
00:08:44,333 --> 00:08:45,333
- [Geng-ming] Hey!
- Hey!

183
00:08:46,166 --> 00:08:47,832
We know what we're doing.

184
00:08:47,833 --> 00:08:49,500
- Take him away.
- [A-wan grunts]

185
00:08:50,250 --> 00:08:51,707
- You can't!
- [groans]

186
00:08:51,708 --> 00:08:53,665
- Sir, this is a hospital!
- [man 1] Come on!

187
00:08:53,666 --> 00:08:55,207
- I'm calling security.
- [man 2] Let's go!

188
00:08:55,208 --> 00:08:57,375
- [man 1] Get him up!
- I... Leave her alone!

189
00:08:58,541 --> 00:09:00,583
This patient could die at any moment!

190
00:09:01,375 --> 00:09:03,250
You want to take responsibility for that?

191
00:09:03,875 --> 00:09:05,125
[A-wan groans]

192
00:09:06,250 --> 00:09:07,750
Don't touch my patient.

193
00:09:08,541 --> 00:09:09,374
Get out!

194
00:09:09,375 --> 00:09:10,790
[A-wan grunting]

195
00:09:10,791 --> 00:09:12,624
Yeah, all right. He's yours for now.

196
00:09:12,625 --> 00:09:13,750
Let's go.

197
00:09:15,833 --> 00:09:17,082
[sighs wearily]

198
00:09:17,083 --> 00:09:19,000
- Nurse, are you all right?
- I'm fine.

199
00:09:27,416 --> 00:09:28,540
[Hsiang-chun] Oh, wow.

200
00:09:28,541 --> 00:09:30,415
HR has just announced

201
00:09:30,416 --> 00:09:32,166
the head of ER resigned.

202
00:09:33,291 --> 00:09:35,791
Why would he suddenly resign
for no reason?

203
00:09:36,500 --> 00:09:37,665
[exhales]

204
00:09:37,666 --> 00:09:39,332
Would you believe it if I told you?

205
00:09:39,333 --> 00:09:41,208
He and Director Chang had a big fight.

206
00:09:42,041 --> 00:09:44,165
And then, HR got a call.

207
00:09:44,166 --> 00:09:45,583
I heard it from his secretary.

208
00:09:46,666 --> 00:09:48,416
All because of a stupid argument.

209
00:09:51,833 --> 00:09:53,166
Who'll be in charge of the ER?

210
00:09:53,958 --> 00:09:56,249
Now, there are two deputies in the ER.

211
00:09:56,250 --> 00:09:57,999
Dr. Cheng and Dr. Chou.

212
00:09:58,000 --> 00:09:59,165
- Hm.
- Who do you like?

213
00:09:59,166 --> 00:10:00,999
Please not Dr. Cheng.

214
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:03,082
[chuckles]
It seems pretty obvious.

215
00:10:03,083 --> 00:10:05,291
- Mm-hm.
- Everyone knows the Director's preference.

216
00:10:05,916 --> 00:10:06,750
Meaning?

217
00:10:07,333 --> 00:10:09,165
What preference would the director have?

218
00:10:09,166 --> 00:10:11,375
[Hsiu-ju] What? How could you miss it?

219
00:10:12,375 --> 00:10:13,832
Who does his daughter give

220
00:10:13,833 --> 00:10:15,625
coffees to here, every day?

221
00:10:16,416 --> 00:10:18,165
- You mean Chou?
- Right?

222
00:10:18,166 --> 00:10:20,124
I always thought Chou liked Dr. He.

223
00:10:20,125 --> 00:10:21,165
Therein lies the problem.

224
00:10:21,166 --> 00:10:23,249
How do you know
Dr. Chou doesn't like Ms. Chang?

225
00:10:23,250 --> 00:10:24,832
She's the daughter of the Director.

226
00:10:24,833 --> 00:10:26,374
I'd sure be happy to be his son-in-law.

227
00:10:26,375 --> 00:10:27,499
[chuckles]

228
00:10:27,500 --> 00:10:29,499
Some pigs ought to look in the mirror.

229
00:10:29,500 --> 00:10:32,415
You look like that
and want to be his son-in-law?

230
00:10:32,416 --> 00:10:33,749
Someone used to think it was okay.

231
00:10:33,750 --> 00:10:35,249
Who knew pigs could talk?

232
00:10:35,250 --> 00:10:37,165
Someone even said pork was her favorite.

233
00:10:37,166 --> 00:10:38,208
[scoffs]

234
00:10:39,250 --> 00:10:40,124
So immature.

235
00:10:40,125 --> 00:10:41,458
[both] Hah!

236
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:44,208
[laughs]

237
00:10:56,041 --> 00:10:57,041
Can I help you?

238
00:10:58,291 --> 00:10:59,415
Director Chung.

239
00:10:59,416 --> 00:11:00,457
I'm sorry.

240
00:11:00,458 --> 00:11:02,665
I saw your door open. I just came in.

241
00:11:02,666 --> 00:11:03,832
It's fine.

242
00:11:03,833 --> 00:11:05,666
I'm not Director of the ER anymore.

243
00:11:06,791 --> 00:11:08,415
I'm almost finished packing up.

244
00:11:08,416 --> 00:11:09,833
This is the last trip.

245
00:11:10,458 --> 00:11:11,290
[exhales]

246
00:11:11,291 --> 00:11:12,416
Dr. Chung.

247
00:11:13,125 --> 00:11:14,665
Come and talk
to your colleagues in the ER.

248
00:11:14,666 --> 00:11:15,582
DIRECTOR, CHUNG SHENG-SHAN

249
00:11:15,583 --> 00:11:17,083
Nobody thinks this is fair.

250
00:11:19,333 --> 00:11:20,500
[inhales deeply]

251
00:11:21,833 --> 00:11:22,958
Cheng-chun.

252
00:11:24,708 --> 00:11:26,000
Am I a good physician?

253
00:11:26,625 --> 00:11:27,583
Or a bad one?

254
00:11:29,750 --> 00:11:30,832
[Hsueh-hung] <i>Well done, Chung.</i>

255
00:11:30,833 --> 00:11:32,582
Here, give this a try.

256
00:11:32,583 --> 00:11:34,583
- Mountain Oolong tea.
- Thank you, Director.

257
00:11:38,125 --> 00:11:39,124
How is it?

258
00:11:39,125 --> 00:11:40,208
Mmm, good!

259
00:11:40,666 --> 00:11:41,625
This tea,

260
00:11:42,291 --> 00:11:44,415
cost $2000 a pound.

261
00:11:44,416 --> 00:11:46,125
It can be steeped three times.

262
00:11:46,583 --> 00:11:47,958
Five times at the most.

263
00:11:48,708 --> 00:11:49,750
Your cup there,

264
00:11:50,250 --> 00:11:51,083
is the sixth steep.

265
00:11:52,166 --> 00:11:53,791
The tea is bland and flavorless.

266
00:11:54,500 --> 00:11:56,458
Just like a regular pound of tea.

267
00:11:57,208 --> 00:11:58,832
That only cost a few dollars.

268
00:11:58,833 --> 00:12:00,208
[pensive music playing]

269
00:12:00,875 --> 00:12:01,833
Dr. Chung.

270
00:12:03,125 --> 00:12:05,333
Lots of things are like drinking tea.

271
00:12:06,041 --> 00:12:07,375
It can't be forced.

272
00:12:08,291 --> 00:12:10,790
No matter how the process is optimized,

273
00:12:10,791 --> 00:12:13,166
or how high the standards are.

274
00:12:13,583 --> 00:12:16,208
You can't always make something better.

275
00:12:20,375 --> 00:12:22,082
Well, time to get rid of this tea.

276
00:12:22,083 --> 00:12:24,124
And make some other adjustments.

277
00:12:24,125 --> 00:12:26,415
The staff levels in the ER,

278
00:12:26,416 --> 00:12:28,332
have always exceeded
the minimum

279
00:12:28,333 --> 00:12:30,249
requirements
for accreditation.

280
00:12:30,250 --> 00:12:31,540
Director.

281
00:12:31,541 --> 00:12:33,332
Sir, it's so crowded in the ER.

282
00:12:33,333 --> 00:12:35,415
The patient to care ratio is at maximum.

283
00:12:35,416 --> 00:12:37,000
They can't go any faster.

284
00:12:38,916 --> 00:12:40,458
And you're telling me you want more?

285
00:12:48,333 --> 00:12:49,958
If you're letting staff go,

286
00:12:50,708 --> 00:12:51,708
I will leave.

287
00:12:56,791 --> 00:12:57,708
I do know

288
00:12:58,333 --> 00:12:59,666
that you looked out for us all.

289
00:13:00,375 --> 00:13:02,125
Protecting us from the pressure above.

290
00:13:02,875 --> 00:13:05,291
And although you and I
didn't always agree,

291
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:08,040
you will always have my respect, Doctor.

292
00:13:08,041 --> 00:13:09,000
Truly.

293
00:13:15,208 --> 00:13:16,791
Okay, come with me.

294
00:13:20,208 --> 00:13:23,665
This area was originally slated
for ER expansion,

295
00:13:23,666 --> 00:13:26,500
Emergency OR and pediatric treatment.

296
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:29,499
But the hospital
amended its operational strategy

297
00:13:29,500 --> 00:13:30,915
due to financial constraints.

298
00:13:30,916 --> 00:13:32,791
So it became what you see here.

299
00:13:33,500 --> 00:13:34,958
Because the ER runs at a loss?

300
00:13:35,583 --> 00:13:37,165
If you and I were in business,

301
00:13:37,166 --> 00:13:39,750
maybe we'd make
the same decision as they did here.

302
00:13:41,541 --> 00:13:42,790
[sighs] Cheng-chun.

303
00:13:42,791 --> 00:13:44,290
In the ER,

304
00:13:44,291 --> 00:13:46,665
there were compromises and trade-offs but...

305
00:13:46,666 --> 00:13:49,333
I was always committed
to the medical professionals.

306
00:13:51,083 --> 00:13:52,333
All these years,

307
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:54,665
I've seen how you wanted

308
00:13:54,666 --> 00:13:55,916
to improve the system.

309
00:13:57,125 --> 00:13:59,541
You need to understand,
the director always wins.

310
00:14:00,291 --> 00:14:03,124
The grim reaper isn't the only one
we have to contend with.

311
00:14:03,125 --> 00:14:04,500
[somber music playing]

312
00:14:05,541 --> 00:14:06,541
[sighs]

313
00:14:09,541 --> 00:14:10,583
That's a good reminder.

314
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:13,291
I'll leave the ER to you.

315
00:14:13,875 --> 00:14:14,708
Keep it up.

316
00:14:15,250 --> 00:14:16,083
All right, then.

317
00:14:25,958 --> 00:14:27,333
[sighs] This is his chart.

318
00:14:29,666 --> 00:14:31,791
- PaO2 okay?
- [Geng-ming] Yes.

319
00:14:32,291 --> 00:14:34,207
But his oxygen SATS are about 85.

320
00:14:34,208 --> 00:14:35,415
<i>And another thing,</i>

321
00:14:35,416 --> 00:14:37,125
<i>his blood is chocolate-colored.</i>

322
00:14:37,375 --> 00:14:38,832
- [cell phone buzzing]
- Chocolate?

323
00:14:38,833 --> 00:14:39,958
Oh, it's his friend now.

324
00:14:42,250 --> 00:14:44,290
<i>Dr. Lin. I'm here at the factory.</i>

325
00:14:44,291 --> 00:14:45,250
<i>Check it out.</i>

326
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:47,165
<i>This is it.</i>

327
00:14:47,166 --> 00:14:48,833
<i>We usually drink and chat here.</i>

328
00:14:50,375 --> 00:14:51,833
<i>The coffee's right there.</i>

329
00:14:53,875 --> 00:14:55,375
Hang on. Go left a bit.

330
00:14:56,458 --> 00:14:57,832
What are those bags?

331
00:14:57,833 --> 00:14:58,790
<i>What, this?</i>

332
00:14:58,791 --> 00:15:00,749
<i>This is for getting rust off machines.</i>

333
00:15:00,750 --> 00:15:01,915
<i>Is there a problem?</i>

334
00:15:01,916 --> 00:15:03,041
Ha! Ha, ha!

335
00:15:04,500 --> 00:15:06,083
He's got nitrite poisoning.

336
00:15:07,333 --> 00:15:08,665
Give him intravenous methylene blue.

337
00:15:08,666 --> 00:15:09,583
- Hurry.
- Okay.

338
00:15:10,125 --> 00:15:12,083
<i>Buddy, I'm hanging up.
You've been a big help. Bye bye.</i>

339
00:15:12,791 --> 00:15:15,415
When he starts to improve a little,
get him up to the OR.

340
00:15:15,416 --> 00:15:16,875
- Thank you, Doctor.
- Mm-hm.

341
00:15:20,208 --> 00:15:21,041
Dr. He.

342
00:15:21,500 --> 00:15:22,999
I hope your trial goes okay.

343
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:24,083
Hmm.

344
00:15:25,291 --> 00:15:26,957
- [chuckles softly]
- [curtains close]

345
00:15:26,958 --> 00:15:28,290
[nurse] Can you hold this for me?

346
00:15:28,291 --> 00:15:30,124
That's what I mean.
Why'd you ask me to do this?

347
00:15:30,125 --> 00:15:31,832
[Mr. Hsu] Can you just handle it
for Godsakes?

348
00:15:31,833 --> 00:15:33,457
I don't know what you
expect me to do, you--

349
00:15:33,458 --> 00:15:35,125
- You're his employer? Stand back.
- Okay.

350
00:15:35,875 --> 00:15:37,040
Hey, doc.

351
00:15:37,041 --> 00:15:38,999
You know, whatever he did,
it was his fault.

352
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:40,374
It has nothing to do with me.

353
00:15:40,375 --> 00:15:42,207
I didn't force him to come to work, right?

354
00:15:42,208 --> 00:15:43,499
He said he wanted to earn more.

355
00:15:43,500 --> 00:15:45,290
- I did him a favor.
- So you know his name then?

356
00:15:45,291 --> 00:15:46,582
He-- He is...

357
00:15:46,583 --> 00:15:48,916
Oh, the agency handles that... yeah.

358
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:51,790
What do you mean, me? Huh?

359
00:15:51,791 --> 00:15:53,499
Are you trying to wash your hands of this?

360
00:15:53,500 --> 00:15:54,915
[Ming-jen] Don't give me that.

361
00:15:54,916 --> 00:15:56,082
Just take him away.

362
00:15:56,083 --> 00:15:58,458
- Why am I even here?
- Handle it, will you?

363
00:15:59,250 --> 00:16:01,500
How he came to be
working for you is one thing.

364
00:16:02,125 --> 00:16:04,790
But A-wan got injured
because you took the easy way out.

365
00:16:04,791 --> 00:16:06,541
Hey, hey, don't speak to me like that.

366
00:16:07,041 --> 00:16:08,375
[sighs]

367
00:16:09,916 --> 00:16:10,791
You see?

368
00:16:11,291 --> 00:16:13,249
Aside from the mess and the chaos,

369
00:16:13,250 --> 00:16:15,290
your chemicals are not stored safely.

370
00:16:15,291 --> 00:16:16,290
The bag is torn.

371
00:16:16,291 --> 00:16:17,915
The powder went into his coffee.

372
00:16:17,916 --> 00:16:19,957
It was nitrite poisoning
that made him dizzy.

373
00:16:19,958 --> 00:16:20,915
So...

374
00:16:20,916 --> 00:16:22,999
- You'll be responsible for the accident.
- But that--

375
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:24,999
That's why he got his hand
caught in the machine.

376
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:27,207
Ah, that. No. Well...

377
00:16:27,208 --> 00:16:29,540
But I-- Can I explain? I just...

378
00:16:29,541 --> 00:16:30,583
[groans]

379
00:16:31,916 --> 00:16:33,375
I can help you make it right.

380
00:16:41,583 --> 00:16:42,750
Is this settled now?

381
00:16:46,375 --> 00:16:47,749
[soft music playing]

382
00:16:47,750 --> 00:16:48,916
[sighs]

383
00:16:49,791 --> 00:16:50,625
Doctor.

384
00:16:52,416 --> 00:16:53,333
Thank you.

385
00:16:54,208 --> 00:16:55,665
No worries, it's my job.

386
00:16:55,666 --> 00:16:57,541
You know, you saved a life.

387
00:16:58,250 --> 00:16:59,916
How can I repay that, huh?

388
00:17:00,583 --> 00:17:01,457
You're my buddy.

389
00:17:01,458 --> 00:17:02,957
[chuckles]

390
00:17:02,958 --> 00:17:04,790
Then find a job and quit drinking.

391
00:17:04,791 --> 00:17:05,750
I know it's hard.

392
00:17:06,625 --> 00:17:07,707
That's how you repay me.

393
00:17:07,708 --> 00:17:09,624
Yes, sir! Buddy.

394
00:17:09,625 --> 00:17:11,166
[both chuckling]

395
00:17:12,666 --> 00:17:13,625
[clears throat]

396
00:17:15,666 --> 00:17:17,290
So, Dr. Lin.

397
00:17:17,291 --> 00:17:19,041
You think you're here to be a hero?

398
00:17:19,416 --> 00:17:21,749
Let me remind you. You're a doctor.

399
00:17:21,750 --> 00:17:23,416
Is this really appropriate?

400
00:17:25,166 --> 00:17:26,625
And to you, sir.

401
00:17:27,208 --> 00:17:28,082
This is a hospital.

402
00:17:28,083 --> 00:17:29,208
If you're not sick,

403
00:17:29,791 --> 00:17:30,874
please leave.

404
00:17:30,875 --> 00:17:32,708
Maybe try the bar down the road.

405
00:17:33,916 --> 00:17:35,124
Dr. Cheng.

406
00:17:35,125 --> 00:17:36,625
Do you have to make him feel bad?

407
00:17:37,666 --> 00:17:40,165
Uh... Don't be angry.

408
00:17:40,166 --> 00:17:42,124
Ah... don't argue.

409
00:17:42,125 --> 00:17:44,750
It's not worth it for someone like me.
I-- I'm just like a fart.

410
00:17:45,208 --> 00:17:46,875
Poof and I'm gone. I'm gone.

411
00:17:50,416 --> 00:17:51,666
You need to watch your attitude.

412
00:17:56,500 --> 00:17:57,833
[sighs wearily]

413
00:18:02,750 --> 00:18:04,790
- Tough day today.
- It's my job.

414
00:18:04,791 --> 00:18:07,582
The new information
Dr. Chou provided is very helpful.

415
00:18:07,583 --> 00:18:08,916
Let's hope for the best.

416
00:18:09,666 --> 00:18:10,790
What information?

417
00:18:10,791 --> 00:18:11,750
[Ms. Yang] Mr. Hung.

418
00:18:12,333 --> 00:18:13,666
We meet again.

419
00:18:17,166 --> 00:18:18,665
It's almost time. Should we go in?

420
00:18:18,666 --> 00:18:19,625
Uh, yeah.

421
00:18:22,375 --> 00:18:23,957
[pensive music playing]

422
00:18:23,958 --> 00:18:25,957
PROSECUTOR'S SEAT

423
00:18:25,958 --> 00:18:27,540
The complainant, Yu Ching-hsiang,

424
00:18:27,541 --> 00:18:30,750
has filed a case of negligent homicide
against the defendant, He Yu-hua.

425
00:18:31,208 --> 00:18:32,125
Mr. Yu?

426
00:18:32,750 --> 00:18:35,166
Can you please tell us
what happened that night?

427
00:18:36,791 --> 00:18:38,458
PRESIDING JUDGE, CHOU YU-KUAN

428
00:18:40,083 --> 00:18:41,875
So it was after 11:00 and...

429
00:18:43,041 --> 00:18:44,541
my wife didn't feel so good.

430
00:18:45,125 --> 00:18:46,916
We went to the hospital's ER.

431
00:18:47,791 --> 00:18:50,000
- My stomach, I'm nauseous.
<i>- And they did some examinations.</i>

432
00:18:50,958 --> 00:18:51,874
[Yu-hua] Ms. Lin.

433
00:18:51,875 --> 00:18:53,125
- Doctor.
- Hm.

434
00:18:53,750 --> 00:18:55,124
You're a little dehydrated.

435
00:18:55,125 --> 00:18:56,415
I'll give you an antiemetic.

436
00:18:56,416 --> 00:18:57,999
Then all of a sudden,

437
00:18:58,000 --> 00:19:00,208
she started having convulsions.

438
00:19:00,791 --> 00:19:02,291
<i>Next thing, she was unconscious.</i>

439
00:19:03,458 --> 00:19:04,332
[doctor] <i>It's eclampsia.</i>

440
00:19:04,333 --> 00:19:06,250
[Ching-hsiang] <i>When the OBGYN came,</i>

441
00:19:06,375 --> 00:19:07,832
<i>she said it was eclampsia.</i>

442
00:19:07,833 --> 00:19:10,832
<i>Dr. Yu-Hua said
she needed an emergency C-section.</i>

443
00:19:10,833 --> 00:19:13,249
<i>And in the end, we lost our child.</i>

444
00:19:13,250 --> 00:19:14,749
[monitor beeping]

445
00:19:14,750 --> 00:19:17,458
<i>And then my wife died
right after the C-section.</i>

446
00:19:21,708 --> 00:19:23,916
I trusted her with my family's lives.

447
00:19:24,541 --> 00:19:26,790
My wife was okay
when we got to the hospital.

448
00:19:26,791 --> 00:19:28,457
And now they're both dead.

449
00:19:28,458 --> 00:19:29,750
Two lives were lost.

450
00:19:30,625 --> 00:19:31,666
They're gone!

451
00:19:32,208 --> 00:19:33,750
It's your fault, they're dead!

452
00:19:35,208 --> 00:19:36,582
A question for the defendant.

453
00:19:36,583 --> 00:19:38,457
What was the patient's condition
that night?

454
00:19:38,458 --> 00:19:39,790
[inhales]

455
00:19:39,791 --> 00:19:41,665
[somber music playing]

456
00:19:41,666 --> 00:19:44,415
The patient
was a 38-year-old pregnant woman.

457
00:19:44,416 --> 00:19:47,332
Dizzy, unwell, also high blood pressure.

458
00:19:47,333 --> 00:19:49,750
- How long have you been in pain?
- [Yu-chuan] Two to three hours.

459
00:19:50,458 --> 00:19:52,833
[Yu-hua] <i>My initial suspicion
was pre-eclampsia.</i>

460
00:19:53,375 --> 00:19:55,290
<i>Then her condition quickly deteriorated</i>

461
00:19:55,291 --> 00:19:57,332
<i>and she started experiencing seizures.</i>

462
00:19:57,333 --> 00:19:58,999
Anti-convulsant injected.

463
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:01,374
[Yu-hua] After administering
an anticonvulsant,

464
00:20:01,375 --> 00:20:02,999
I consulted the OBGYN.

465
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:06,124
And why is it that you didn't
immediately order a CT scan?

466
00:20:06,125 --> 00:20:07,665
The baby's heart rate

467
00:20:07,666 --> 00:20:09,582
was already at a dangerous level.

468
00:20:09,583 --> 00:20:10,999
What that called for,

469
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:12,708
was an emergency C-section.

470
00:20:13,625 --> 00:20:14,541
Your Honor.

471
00:20:15,291 --> 00:20:16,249
DEFENSE COUNSEL'S SEAT

472
00:20:16,250 --> 00:20:17,541
According to the autopsy,

473
00:20:18,250 --> 00:20:20,124
Lin Yu-chuan had a brain stem hemorrhage.

474
00:20:20,125 --> 00:20:21,749
We'd like to submit
two pieces of evidence.

475
00:20:21,750 --> 00:20:22,791
PRESIDING JUDGE, CHOU YU-KUAN

476
00:20:25,208 --> 00:20:26,624
The defense would like to submit

477
00:20:26,625 --> 00:20:28,332
these two studies from renowned journals.

478
00:20:28,333 --> 00:20:29,499
PLAINTIFF'S SEAT

479
00:20:29,500 --> 00:20:32,290
The first is about differential diagnosis
of brain stem hemorrhage.

480
00:20:32,291 --> 00:20:34,874
The second is about
the standard guidelines

481
00:20:34,875 --> 00:20:36,707
for the treatment of pre-eclampsia.

482
00:20:36,708 --> 00:20:38,499
The conclusions of these papers indicate,

483
00:20:38,500 --> 00:20:41,582
that pre-eclampsia can potentially cause
brain stem hemorrhage,

484
00:20:41,583 --> 00:20:43,582
where mortality is extremely high.

485
00:20:43,583 --> 00:20:46,290
In cases where a pregnant woman
with pre-eclampsia

486
00:20:46,291 --> 00:20:49,915
has complications such as seizures
and a drop in fetal heart rate,

487
00:20:49,916 --> 00:20:52,957
an emergency C-section
is the priority treatment option.

488
00:20:52,958 --> 00:20:54,415
In other words,

489
00:20:54,416 --> 00:20:57,790
Dr. He's handling of the situation
was standard medical practice.

490
00:20:57,791 --> 00:21:00,040
Therefore, there is no direct causal link

491
00:21:00,041 --> 00:21:02,375
between the patient's death
and the defendant.

492
00:21:03,291 --> 00:21:04,916
[intense music playing]

493
00:21:11,625 --> 00:21:13,999
PLAINTIFF'S SEAT

494
00:21:14,000 --> 00:21:16,582
[Yu-Hsuan] Your Honor,
we'd also like to submit a document.

495
00:21:16,583 --> 00:21:17,499
Okay.

496
00:21:17,500 --> 00:21:20,290
This outlines Dr. He's
duty roster in the hospital.

497
00:21:20,291 --> 00:21:21,374
DEFENDANT AND ASSISTING PERSON,
DEFENDANT AND AGENT

498
00:21:21,375 --> 00:21:22,874
Will the defendant confirm,

499
00:21:22,875 --> 00:21:24,374
that on February 3rd,

500
00:21:24,375 --> 00:21:27,416
the day before the incident,
you also had a shift, is that right?

501
00:21:28,666 --> 00:21:29,665
Sure.

502
00:21:29,666 --> 00:21:31,165
Well, based on these records,

503
00:21:31,166 --> 00:21:33,250
it seems that on February 2nd,

504
00:21:33,791 --> 00:21:35,582
you worked 17 hours.

505
00:21:35,583 --> 00:21:36,875
Is that information correct?

506
00:21:37,666 --> 00:21:38,499
That sounds right.

507
00:21:38,500 --> 00:21:39,790
And you often stay late

508
00:21:39,791 --> 00:21:42,249
or get there early
to take classes for new doctors.

509
00:21:42,250 --> 00:21:43,166
Have I got that right?

510
00:21:43,625 --> 00:21:44,458
That's correct.

511
00:21:45,458 --> 00:21:46,875
So working all that overtime,

512
00:21:47,375 --> 00:21:49,249
does it affect
your judgment with patients?

513
00:21:49,250 --> 00:21:50,166
[exhales]

514
00:21:50,625 --> 00:21:52,583
That's just the job in the ER.

515
00:21:53,083 --> 00:21:54,375
Working long hours,

516
00:21:55,333 --> 00:21:56,707
is normal.

517
00:21:56,708 --> 00:21:59,249
Being the attending physician
for a very sick patient,

518
00:21:59,250 --> 00:22:01,082
the responsibility is mine.

519
00:22:01,083 --> 00:22:02,624
Well it sounds like you think

520
00:22:02,625 --> 00:22:04,875
working overtime is a very noble thing.

521
00:22:06,458 --> 00:22:09,040
Would the defendant be okay
if a driver doing overtime,

522
00:22:09,041 --> 00:22:10,582
had a bus load of passengers?

523
00:22:10,583 --> 00:22:11,999
Would that be acceptable?

524
00:22:12,000 --> 00:22:14,415
Or is it just a patient putting herself

525
00:22:14,416 --> 00:22:15,999
in this doctor's hands,

526
00:22:16,000 --> 00:22:17,707
was a recipe for disaster

527
00:22:17,708 --> 00:22:19,208
and a reminder of the tragic risks.

528
00:22:19,916 --> 00:22:21,707
- I...
- [inhales]

529
00:22:21,708 --> 00:22:23,790
[intense music playing]

530
00:22:23,791 --> 00:22:25,916
[sighs wearily]

531
00:22:43,208 --> 00:22:45,415
[Yu-Hsuan] <i>A patient putting herself
in this doctor's hands</i>

532
00:22:45,416 --> 00:22:46,874
<i>was a recipe for disaster</i>

533
00:22:46,875 --> 00:22:49,415
<i>and a reminder of the tragic risks.</i>

534
00:22:49,416 --> 00:22:50,790
[Ching-hsiang] <i>Two lives were lost.</i>

535
00:22:50,791 --> 00:22:52,125
<i>It's your fault they're dead.</i>

536
00:22:58,416 --> 00:23:00,833
[rain pattering]

537
00:23:06,916 --> 00:23:09,083
[somber music playing]

538
00:23:26,958 --> 00:23:28,916
I really didn't want to show up today.

539
00:23:33,708 --> 00:23:35,250
Because I'm scared.

540
00:23:37,875 --> 00:23:39,166
I'm so afraid

541
00:23:40,500 --> 00:23:41,666
of seeing the man

542
00:23:42,791 --> 00:23:44,875
who lost his wife and child.

543
00:23:45,916 --> 00:23:47,791
And I have to say things like,

544
00:23:50,625 --> 00:23:52,500
"procedures were followed".

545
00:23:53,541 --> 00:23:54,707
[sobs]

546
00:23:54,708 --> 00:23:56,666
I even have to take

547
00:23:57,291 --> 00:23:59,333
studies and papers to prove

548
00:24:00,333 --> 00:24:03,041
that they were probably
going to die anyway.

549
00:24:05,833 --> 00:24:08,290
[cries]

550
00:24:08,291 --> 00:24:09,957
It doesn't seem right.

551
00:24:09,958 --> 00:24:12,333
[sniffles]

552
00:24:16,250 --> 00:24:17,707
What am I saying?

553
00:24:17,708 --> 00:24:19,666
What am I? Ah...

554
00:24:20,875 --> 00:24:22,582
I just know...

555
00:24:22,583 --> 00:24:25,249
I'm the worst doctor in the world now.

556
00:24:25,250 --> 00:24:27,416
[cries]

557
00:24:30,208 --> 00:24:31,875
[melancholy music playing]

558
00:24:33,666 --> 00:24:34,541
Yu-hua.

559
00:24:36,500 --> 00:24:38,500
You've got nothing to feel ashamed of.

560
00:24:39,916 --> 00:24:40,750
Truly.

561
00:24:48,166 --> 00:24:51,125
[cries louder]

562
00:25:15,125 --> 00:25:15,958
Cheng-chun.

563
00:25:16,583 --> 00:25:19,208
The papers you gave the lawyer...

564
00:25:20,166 --> 00:25:21,041
Thank you.

565
00:25:22,125 --> 00:25:23,208
Well, don't thank me.

566
00:25:23,875 --> 00:25:25,249
You know who I found asleep

567
00:25:25,250 --> 00:25:27,625
when I got to the hospital this morning?

568
00:25:29,166 --> 00:25:30,083
Geng-ming.

569
00:25:30,708 --> 00:25:31,832
He, Tung-yen, and Tang Hsi,

570
00:25:31,833 --> 00:25:33,583
stayed up all night to find that stuff.

571
00:25:34,791 --> 00:25:36,166
They support you all the way.

572
00:25:37,291 --> 00:25:39,208
You ever need help, just ask.

573
00:25:41,083 --> 00:25:42,000
Oh.

574
00:25:42,708 --> 00:25:43,583
Okay.

575
00:25:44,583 --> 00:25:45,541
And another thing.

576
00:25:46,166 --> 00:25:47,875
You're not the worst doctor in the world.

577
00:25:48,916 --> 00:25:51,082
You're probably the second best I know.

578
00:25:51,083 --> 00:25:53,040
[somber music playing]

579
00:25:53,041 --> 00:25:54,416
[chuckles]

580
00:25:55,125 --> 00:25:56,666
And, the best doctor is?

581
00:25:57,875 --> 00:25:58,708
Hm?

582
00:26:01,083 --> 00:26:02,416
Not gonna fall for it.

583
00:26:02,875 --> 00:26:03,833
[laughs]

584
00:26:06,541 --> 00:26:07,708
[sighs]

585
00:26:18,666 --> 00:26:20,375
- Where is he?
- I don't know.

586
00:26:22,583 --> 00:26:23,665
[Geng-ming] Hey!

587
00:26:23,666 --> 00:26:26,040
Welcome to my big singing contest.

588
00:26:26,041 --> 00:26:27,583
Why did you want us to come here?

589
00:26:27,916 --> 00:26:29,165
Can't work colleagues get together?

590
00:26:29,166 --> 00:26:31,165
- I'm out of here.
- I'll get us a ride.

591
00:26:31,166 --> 00:26:32,540
Hey, wait, wait, wait. No, no, no.

592
00:26:32,541 --> 00:26:33,790
You don't want to leave now.

593
00:26:33,791 --> 00:26:35,790
- You'll miss out on a special guest.
- Like?

594
00:26:35,791 --> 00:26:37,165
LOVE THE BLIND

595
00:26:37,166 --> 00:26:38,125
My dad!

596
00:26:38,666 --> 00:26:40,207
Hey! Hey, hey.

597
00:26:40,208 --> 00:26:42,290
You must be workmates of my boy, huh?

598
00:26:42,291 --> 00:26:43,625
- Hello.
- That's right!

599
00:26:44,375 --> 00:26:45,832
Oh. Ah.

600
00:26:45,833 --> 00:26:48,040
- You're Tang Hsi, huh?
- Oh, yeah!

601
00:26:48,041 --> 00:26:49,499
You must be beautiful. I--

602
00:26:49,500 --> 00:26:51,207
You know, I heard so much about you

603
00:26:51,208 --> 00:26:52,957
- from my son.
- [Geng-ming] Yeah.

604
00:26:52,958 --> 00:26:54,874
I thought you'll end up being his wife.

605
00:26:54,875 --> 00:26:56,665
- Ah! Dad...
- Of course, I'm kidding.

606
00:26:56,666 --> 00:26:57,707
Dad banged his head.

607
00:26:57,708 --> 00:26:59,165
Uh, he's a little foggy.

608
00:26:59,166 --> 00:27:00,790
- Have a seat, anywhere.
- Okay.

609
00:27:00,791 --> 00:27:01,790
Dad, what are you doing?

610
00:27:01,791 --> 00:27:03,207
- [Geng-ming] Help yourselves.
- Hi!

611
00:27:03,208 --> 00:27:04,374
Hey, hi, Hsiang-chun.

612
00:27:04,375 --> 00:27:05,291
[both] Hi.

613
00:27:06,541 --> 00:27:08,375
That's... A different look.

614
00:27:09,583 --> 00:27:10,749
Oh, I...

615
00:27:10,750 --> 00:27:12,874
What's the matter? Do I look messy?

616
00:27:12,875 --> 00:27:13,832
I just dressed up today.

617
00:27:13,833 --> 00:27:14,750
I don't know.

618
00:27:15,250 --> 00:27:16,500
Came along to see everyone.

619
00:27:17,750 --> 00:27:19,166
You don't like what I'm wearing?

620
00:27:20,083 --> 00:27:21,333
Well, I'll get drinks.

621
00:27:25,916 --> 00:27:27,332
[crowd applauding]

622
00:27:27,333 --> 00:27:29,249
- [Dad] Hi thank you, thank you.
- Mom, I'm here.

623
00:27:29,250 --> 00:27:30,749
As many people here know,

624
00:27:30,750 --> 00:27:32,708
I was born blind.

625
00:27:33,333 --> 00:27:34,540
And of course,

626
00:27:34,541 --> 00:27:35,999
I depended on my wife

627
00:27:36,000 --> 00:27:39,415
for all sorts of important tasks
in my day to day.

628
00:27:39,416 --> 00:27:42,874
She took great care of me
and Wei-sung was her favorite singer.

629
00:27:42,875 --> 00:27:44,291
I'd like to think of this

630
00:27:44,875 --> 00:27:46,583
as fulfilling her last wish.

631
00:27:47,125 --> 00:27:47,957
Okay...

632
00:27:47,958 --> 00:27:49,791
- [man cheers]
- Thank you, thank you.

633
00:27:50,916 --> 00:27:52,333
While I'm thinking about my son,

634
00:27:53,458 --> 00:27:56,541
he's always felt responsible
for his mother's death.

635
00:27:57,166 --> 00:27:59,874
He would hide under the altar crying
and then try to

636
00:27:59,875 --> 00:28:00,833
blame himself.

637
00:28:02,083 --> 00:28:04,958
So, I'd play Wei Sung's tunes for him.

638
00:28:06,041 --> 00:28:07,374
To comfort him.

639
00:28:07,375 --> 00:28:09,958
And let him know
everything was going to be okay.

640
00:28:10,958 --> 00:28:12,332
Everyone here

641
00:28:12,333 --> 00:28:15,083
has at least one of Wei Sung's tunes
in their heart.

642
00:28:16,125 --> 00:28:18,249
Anyway, I've taken up
enough of all of your time.

643
00:28:18,250 --> 00:28:20,832
Let's eat and drink
and enjoy each other's company, eh?

644
00:28:20,833 --> 00:28:22,499
[crowd cheering]

645
00:28:22,500 --> 00:28:24,040
Okay, okay. And maybe right now...

646
00:28:24,041 --> 00:28:25,875
We can sing a little too.

647
00:28:27,541 --> 00:28:29,541
[acoustic music playing]

648
00:28:30,750 --> 00:28:32,208
LOVE THE BLIND

649
00:28:32,625 --> 00:28:33,957
- [sister] Dad.
- [Dad] Huh?

650
00:28:33,958 --> 00:28:35,207
That guy looks like Wei Sung.

651
00:28:35,208 --> 00:28:36,332
Wei Sung, no way.

652
00:28:36,333 --> 00:28:37,665
- [man] Wei Sung?
- [woman] It is.

653
00:28:37,666 --> 00:28:38,707
- That's him.
- Is that him?

654
00:28:38,708 --> 00:28:39,874
- It's Wei Sung.
- Oh, my God.

655
00:28:39,875 --> 00:28:41,457
- It's him!
- Wei-Sung is here.

656
00:28:41,458 --> 00:28:43,541
[sister] Wei Sung is here. It's Wei Sung.

657
00:28:44,208 --> 00:28:45,415
- Dad!
- Well, where is he?

658
00:28:45,416 --> 00:28:46,582
Wei Sung is here!

659
00:28:46,583 --> 00:28:47,749
Is that you, Wei Sung?

660
00:28:47,750 --> 00:28:49,915
Hey. Hey, it's true.

661
00:28:49,916 --> 00:28:52,790
- [Dad] Hey. Hey there.
- [Wei Sung] Hey. How are you doing there?

662
00:28:52,791 --> 00:28:53,915
Hello there, everyone.

663
00:28:53,916 --> 00:28:56,165
[crowd] Hi!

664
00:28:56,166 --> 00:28:57,499
I'm Wei Sung.

665
00:28:57,500 --> 00:29:00,040
[crowd cheering]

666
00:29:00,041 --> 00:29:01,458
So a while ago,

667
00:29:02,458 --> 00:29:05,208
I got pretty sick, and Dr. Geng-Ming here,

668
00:29:05,833 --> 00:29:06,916
he came to visit me often.

669
00:29:08,250 --> 00:29:10,791
<i>But today, he gave me a precious gift.</i>

670
00:29:11,583 --> 00:29:14,125
<i>In it were notes of encouragement
from all of you.</i>

671
00:29:14,583 --> 00:29:16,249
<i>I was very moved.</i>

672
00:29:16,250 --> 00:29:18,625
<i>And I wanted to come down here
and meet you all.</i>

673
00:29:18,916 --> 00:29:19,916
Hmm.

674
00:29:20,875 --> 00:29:22,832
<i>Among those beautiful notes,</i>

675
00:29:22,833 --> 00:29:24,833
<i>there was one from a person
called Wu Hsiao-li.</i>

676
00:29:25,708 --> 00:29:29,375
<i>She made me remember
the pure joy of singing on stage.</i>

677
00:29:30,166 --> 00:29:31,624
Is Wu Hsiao-li here, please?

678
00:29:31,625 --> 00:29:32,833
[woman 1] Yes! She's here.

679
00:29:33,500 --> 00:29:35,333
I have a small wish to ask her today.

680
00:29:36,208 --> 00:29:37,583
Will you please welcome,

681
00:29:38,083 --> 00:29:40,249
Ms. Wu Hsiao-li
to the stage

682
00:29:40,250 --> 00:29:41,541
to sing a song with me.

683
00:29:42,166 --> 00:29:43,124
[chuckles]

684
00:29:43,125 --> 00:29:45,040
Go, go on, go up there.

685
00:29:45,041 --> 00:29:47,749
- [woman 2] That's great.
- Follow me.

686
00:29:47,750 --> 00:29:50,375
[indistinct chatter]

687
00:29:53,666 --> 00:29:55,499
[acoustic music playing]

688
00:29:55,500 --> 00:29:59,250
<i>♪ As the morning sun rose ♪</i>

689
00:30:01,791 --> 00:30:05,250
<i>♪ I embarked on my journey ♪</i>

690
00:30:07,958 --> 00:30:11,791
<i>♪ Be it dawn or dusk ♪</i>

691
00:30:13,750 --> 00:30:17,791
<i>♪ Save wounded souls ♪</i>

692
00:30:20,333 --> 00:30:23,915
<i>♪ Moving forward through wind and rain ♪</i>

693
00:30:23,916 --> 00:30:26,332
<i>♪ Let dreams continue to blossom ♪</i>

694
00:30:26,333 --> 00:30:28,415
<i>♪ You and I ♪</i>

695
00:30:28,416 --> 00:30:30,832
<i>♪ Join hands to welcome ♪</i>

696
00:30:30,833 --> 00:30:32,707
<i>♪ The sun after the storm ♪</i>

697
00:30:32,708 --> 00:30:34,790
<i>♪ Never give up ♪</i>

698
00:30:34,791 --> 00:30:38,707
<i>♪ Even if it leaves scars of pain ♪</i>

699
00:30:38,708 --> 00:30:40,624
<i>♪ Keep singing ♪</i>

700
00:30:40,625 --> 00:30:43,874
<i>♪ Life's melody ♪</i>

701
00:30:43,875 --> 00:30:47,000
[crowd cheering]

702
00:30:49,041 --> 00:30:51,041
[laughs]

703
00:30:52,583 --> 00:30:55,083
[indistinct chatter]

704
00:31:03,250 --> 00:31:04,166
What's the matter?

705
00:31:04,625 --> 00:31:05,750
Don't you think

706
00:31:06,458 --> 00:31:08,041
that you're different from before?

707
00:31:09,458 --> 00:31:11,082
- Like how?
- [chuckles softly]

708
00:31:11,083 --> 00:31:12,457
I mean, um...

709
00:31:12,458 --> 00:31:14,500
If it were the old you, um...

710
00:31:15,166 --> 00:31:16,750
Would you even be here?

711
00:31:17,125 --> 00:31:18,249
The nurses all think

712
00:31:18,250 --> 00:31:20,291
that you're becoming like Geng-Ming.

713
00:31:20,916 --> 00:31:22,999
- You think so?
- [chuckles softly]

714
00:31:23,000 --> 00:31:26,040
I mean, you guys found the reason
for that patient's fever,

715
00:31:26,041 --> 00:31:29,083
because you decided to be
a busybody like Geng-Ming, right?

716
00:31:29,916 --> 00:31:31,832
I think that now I can see

717
00:31:31,833 --> 00:31:33,540
why he's such a busybody.

718
00:31:33,541 --> 00:31:34,750
Hm?

719
00:31:36,625 --> 00:31:37,874
- Check it out.
- [Dad] All together.

720
00:31:37,875 --> 00:31:40,832
- [sister] All together!
- [cheering]

721
00:31:40,833 --> 00:31:42,665
- Hey!
- [Hsi] Nice moves!

722
00:31:42,666 --> 00:31:43,999
[all laughing]

723
00:31:44,000 --> 00:31:46,583
- [Geng-ming] Watch out, Dad!
- [sister] Take it easy, Dad.

724
00:31:47,666 --> 00:31:49,124
[Hsi] You call that dancing?

725
00:31:49,125 --> 00:31:50,208
No wonder you fell.

726
00:31:51,125 --> 00:31:52,375
Doctor, am I going to live?

727
00:31:52,666 --> 00:31:53,832
[sighs] Oh yes.

728
00:31:53,833 --> 00:31:55,125
You could lose your arm.

729
00:31:55,541 --> 00:31:57,500
Oh. But I'm doing a dancing competition.

730
00:31:58,250 --> 00:31:59,416
You're hilarious.

731
00:31:59,916 --> 00:32:02,208
- You should join a comedy contest.
- [chuckles]

732
00:32:02,625 --> 00:32:03,458
Wait.

733
00:32:05,791 --> 00:32:07,125
[romantic music playing]

734
00:32:13,583 --> 00:32:14,416
[Hsi] Done!

735
00:32:27,333 --> 00:32:28,166
[Ms. Yang] Dr. Lin.

736
00:32:29,500 --> 00:32:30,583
Oh.

737
00:32:34,625 --> 00:32:36,208
My client, Wei Sung,

738
00:32:36,875 --> 00:32:38,583
he's withdrawn his law suit.

739
00:32:39,583 --> 00:32:41,000
Oh. He did?

740
00:32:42,166 --> 00:32:43,707
[Ms. Yang] He wants me to tell you,

741
00:32:43,708 --> 00:32:46,666
his concert was cancelled
primarily due to ticket sales.

742
00:32:47,000 --> 00:32:48,458
His vocal cords are fine.

743
00:32:51,291 --> 00:32:52,165
And thanks...

744
00:32:52,166 --> 00:32:53,250
For the invitation.

745
00:32:53,958 --> 00:32:55,040
We loved it.

746
00:32:55,041 --> 00:32:57,333
[chuckles softly]

747
00:32:58,083 --> 00:32:58,916
Anytime.

748
00:33:00,333 --> 00:33:03,166
[lighthearted music playing]

749
00:33:12,750 --> 00:33:13,583
Okay.

750
00:33:14,083 --> 00:33:14,915
Rest up.

751
00:33:14,916 --> 00:33:16,540
Run a hot bath for a start,

752
00:33:16,541 --> 00:33:18,832
drink a big glass of red,
and get some sleep.

753
00:33:18,833 --> 00:33:19,833
[chuckles softly]

754
00:33:22,041 --> 00:33:23,749
I admit that sounds good.

755
00:33:23,750 --> 00:33:25,000
[chuckles]

756
00:33:26,166 --> 00:33:28,083
[romantic music playing]

757
00:33:35,958 --> 00:33:37,125
[sighs]

758
00:33:41,583 --> 00:33:44,083
[somber music playing]

759
00:33:48,083 --> 00:33:48,916
[Yu-hua] <i>Cheng-chun.</i>

760
00:33:52,208 --> 00:33:54,125
[sighs] Thanks again.

761
00:33:54,666 --> 00:33:55,750
Drive safe.

762
00:34:09,083 --> 00:34:10,916
[laughs]

763
00:34:11,958 --> 00:34:12,790
[gasps]

764
00:34:12,791 --> 00:34:14,583
[brakes screech]

765
00:34:17,208 --> 00:34:18,333
[exhales]

766
00:34:26,833 --> 00:34:28,374
[heart thumping]

767
00:34:28,375 --> 00:34:30,041
<i>Can't I be happy?</i>

768
00:34:31,000 --> 00:34:31,833
<i>Jui?</i>

769
00:34:32,375 --> 00:34:34,833
[monitor beeping rapidly]

770
00:34:35,875 --> 00:34:37,666
[Cheng-chun breathing heavily]

771
00:34:47,166 --> 00:34:48,208
Jui.

772
00:34:49,041 --> 00:34:49,875
[Jui's dad] Jui!

773
00:34:50,333 --> 00:34:51,375
Jui.

774
00:34:52,166 --> 00:34:53,541
Jui, wake up!

775
00:34:54,541 --> 00:34:56,707
[Jui's mom crying]

776
00:34:56,708 --> 00:34:58,166
Why aren't you saving him?

777
00:34:58,833 --> 00:35:00,583
Why are you just standing there?

778
00:35:00,833 --> 00:35:01,666
Do it!

779
00:35:02,625 --> 00:35:03,707
Save my son!

780
00:35:03,708 --> 00:35:04,874
You promised me!

781
00:35:04,875 --> 00:35:07,332
- You promised me you'd save him!
- I'm so sorry.

782
00:35:07,333 --> 00:35:08,999
[cries]

783
00:35:09,000 --> 00:35:11,499
Don't be sorry. I don't want an apology.

784
00:35:11,500 --> 00:35:13,915
- Dr. Chou.
- Stop apologizing! Save him!

785
00:35:13,916 --> 00:35:15,540
- I can't, I'm sorry.
- [Hsiu-ju] Dr. Chou.

786
00:35:15,541 --> 00:35:17,457
We need your assistance immediately.

787
00:35:17,458 --> 00:35:18,999
- Dr. Chou.
- Please!

788
00:35:19,000 --> 00:35:20,124
I'm so sorry.

789
00:35:20,125 --> 00:35:22,082
- Dr. Chou, hurry!
- Come back!

790
00:35:22,083 --> 00:35:23,875
Don't abandon our boy!

791
00:35:30,916 --> 00:35:32,583
[exhales]

792
00:35:37,416 --> 00:35:39,208
My dad and sister wanted to thank you.

793
00:35:39,666 --> 00:35:41,250
Oh. It was fun.

794
00:35:43,375 --> 00:35:45,249
Would you like to come to the next one?

795
00:35:45,250 --> 00:35:46,415
Hm-mm...

796
00:35:46,416 --> 00:35:47,707
That depends on you.

797
00:35:47,708 --> 00:35:50,166
[romantic music playing]

798
00:35:51,000 --> 00:35:51,916
I'll do my best.

799
00:35:52,875 --> 00:35:53,915
[chuckles softly]

800
00:35:53,916 --> 00:35:54,832
Oh. No.

801
00:35:54,833 --> 00:35:57,082
I was thinking about the ER, but...

802
00:35:57,083 --> 00:35:59,415
- That's all!
- [chuckles] What do you mean by that?

803
00:35:59,416 --> 00:36:01,582
Of course you meant work.
What do you think I was saying?

804
00:36:01,583 --> 00:36:03,750
- I didn't think anything.
- Hi!

805
00:36:05,000 --> 00:36:06,457
- Hi!
- [giggles]

806
00:36:06,458 --> 00:36:07,499
Oh.

807
00:36:07,500 --> 00:36:08,540
Hm.

808
00:36:08,541 --> 00:36:10,500
There you go. Cool.

809
00:36:13,166 --> 00:36:14,124
That's two.

810
00:36:14,125 --> 00:36:15,791
- And, that's enough. Okay.
- Here.

811
00:36:17,583 --> 00:36:18,666
He's alone today.

812
00:36:19,208 --> 00:36:20,540
Yeah, his good friend isn't here.

813
00:36:20,541 --> 00:36:22,165
- You could be his friend.
- Yes.

814
00:36:22,166 --> 00:36:23,874
- I'm a cat.
- Ugh.

815
00:36:23,875 --> 00:36:25,750
You're so funny! [laughs]

816
00:36:25,875 --> 00:36:26,958
[alarm beeping]

817
00:36:27,458 --> 00:36:28,707
[meows]

818
00:36:28,708 --> 00:36:30,124
Hey! No! Watch out!

819
00:36:30,125 --> 00:36:31,416
Stop! Come back!

820
00:36:33,041 --> 00:36:33,874
[truck honks]

821
00:36:33,875 --> 00:36:35,000
Tang Hsi!

822
00:36:37,083 --> 00:36:38,125
[ominous music playing]

823
00:36:39,625 --> 00:36:41,415
[gasps]

824
00:36:41,416 --> 00:36:42,874
- [driver] 1-1-9?
- Tang Hsi.

825
00:36:42,875 --> 00:36:44,582
[driver] Hello, I need an ambulance here.

826
00:36:44,583 --> 00:36:45,666
There's been an accident.

827
00:36:46,333 --> 00:36:47,207
Someone's hurt.

828
00:36:47,208 --> 00:36:48,208
Hurry!

829
00:36:48,958 --> 00:36:50,208
[pants]

830
00:36:54,708 --> 00:36:55,540
Tang...

831
00:36:55,541 --> 00:36:56,625
Tang Hsi.

832
00:37:15,708 --> 00:37:17,083
[closing theme music playing]
